CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ two is_constructible queries on one type resolve independently: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
invalid implicit conversion
--
N5008 [dcl.init.ref]/5: a non-const lvalue reference does not bind an rvalue, so
a converting constructor `T(X&)` is not viable for an rvalue argument.
Regression test for two __is_constructible queries on one type (lvalue then
rvalue) where the first instantiates `T(X&)` and the second reached it with an
rvalue, aborting type-checking ("invalid implicit conversion") and dropping the
function body.  Non-vacuous: assertion.2 must FAIL.
